# MI Gas — every variable the site reads. Copy to .env.local for local work; set the real
# values in the hosting dashboard. Never commit a filled-in copy of this file.
#
# House rule, and the reason this file exists: nothing here is a paid service. Mail goes
# over SMTP through a mailbox the client already owns. There is no scheduling account, no
# object store and no mail API, so there is nothing on this list that can send him a bill.

# ── Mail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset SMTP_HOST and the site still works — forms succeed for the visitor and the full
# brief is written to the server log. That is deliberate (a form that errors because of a
# missing env var teaches people it is broken) and it means bookings exist ONLY in the log
# until this is set. Set it before anyone real uses the site.
SMTP_HOST=
# 587 for STARTTLS, 465 for implicit TLS. The code switches `secure` on this number;
# getting it backwards fails by hanging rather than by erroring.
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
# Must be an address that mailbox is allowed to send as. Falls back to SMTP_USER.
SMTP_FROM=

# ── Where enquiries land ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Falls back to SITE.email in lib/site.ts, which is still a PLACEHOLDER — so until one of
# the two is real, notification is skipped and logged.
MIGAS_NOTIFY_TO=

# ── The availability admin, /admin ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The PIN that signs him in to edit his own hours. Unset, the page says plainly that
# it is not switched on. Changing it signs every device out at once.
MIGAS_ADMIN_PIN=

# Written by Vercel when a Blob store is attached to the project (Storage tab, one
# click, free tier). It is where the /admin edits are kept: one small JSON document.
# Unset, the booking grid serves the defaults in lib/site.ts and /admin says edits
# cannot be saved yet. This is Vercel's own storage riding on the hosting he already
# has, not a new vendor — the hobby tier's free allowance covers a one-file store by
# orders of magnitude, and the no-new-bills rule in the README still holds.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ── His calendar, read back ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The private "secret address in iCal format" of his own calendar (Google: Settings >
# your calendar > Integrate; iCloud and Outlook have equivalents). Set, every event on
# his calendar removes the booking slots it covers, which is what closes the
# double-booking loop: a confirmed call lands on his calendar via the emailed invite,
# the feed carries it, the slot disappears. Unset, slots come from the weekly windows
# alone, exactly as before. Recurring calendar events are counted and logged rather
# than expanded — recurring commitments belong in the /admin windows.
# Treat the URL as a secret: anyone holding it can read his calendar.
MIGAS_BUSY_ICS_URL=
